  "worked_solution": "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{\u2032}(t)=2{sec}^{2}\u2061t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{\u2032}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=2{sec}^{2}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=2{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}(t)=\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\operatorname{sec}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\u27e8{x}^{\u2032}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,{y}^{\u2032}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e84,\\,\\sqrt{2}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
